<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aïr Mountains</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aïr Massif</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aïr Mountains are a massif of granite and volcanic highlands in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. They are the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> groups such as the Kel Ewey, and the Sultanate of Agadez lies on their southern edge. They were the main base of the Kaocen revolt of 1916–1917 and are now partly protected as a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/air-mountains.jpg" alt="Aïr Mountains" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Denvermaxwell at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timia_valley.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
